IO-38: take table_tseriesLookup()'s end-of-file shortcut only past the last entry

For a series read from a file, table_tseriesLookup() returned y1, the left
end of the bracket, as soon as feof() was set. When the file's last line has
no line break, the read that returns that line also sets end-of-file while
the bracket is still [second-to-last, last], so every date after the last
entry got the second-to-last value. The same shortcut also answered dates
earlier than the bracket without rewinding the file. Return y2 (the last
entry read) and take the shortcut only for dates after it; earlier dates
fall through to the existing rewind.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-38_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/table.c b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
index c7564d2..7c06356 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/table.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
@@ -768,9 +768,11 @@ double table_tseriesLookup(TTable *table, double x, char extend)
     return table_interpolate(x, table->x1, table->y1, table->x2, table->y2);
     
     // --- end of external time series file has been reached
-    if ( table->file.mode == USE_FILE && feof(table->file.file) )
+    //     (x2 is the file's last entry; earlier dates rewind below)
+    if ( table->file.mode == USE_FILE && feof(table->file.file)
+    &&   x > table->x2 )
     {
-        if (extend == TRUE) return table->y1;
+        if (extend == TRUE) return table->y2;
         else return 0;
     }
 
